-- An IMPORTED infix operator (prelude `is in`) as an operand of a built-in
-- connective, in a module that also declares a LOCAL operator.
--
-- The local operator matters: it makes this module's hint registry non-empty,
-- so the parser's mixfix keyword gate is ACTIVE and `is in` parses only
-- because the import merge supplies its hint. (With no local operator the
-- registry is empty and any identifier chain is accepted permissively, which
-- pins nothing.) The prelude matters too: it wraps everything in `§ Prelude`,
-- so its hints exist only because buildMixfixHintRegistry recurses into
-- sections. Severing either link — the import merge in GetMixfixRegistry, or
-- the section recursion — turns the #EVALs below into loud parse errors
-- ("unexpected `is in`").
IMPORT prelude

@infixl 6
GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE a LOCALOP b IS a MINUS b

#EVAL 3 `is in` (SET OF 1, 2) OR 3 `is in` (SET OF 3, 4)
#EVAL 5 `is in` (SET OF 1, 2) OR 5 `is in` (SET OF 3, 4)
#EVAL 2 `is in` (SET OF 1, 2) AND 3 `is in` (SET OF 3, 4)
#EVAL 10 LOCALOP 3 EQUALS 7 AND 4 `is in` (SET OF 3, 4)
